<title>UK: Big ferry groups urge French blockade injunction.</title>
<headline>Big ferry groups urge French blockade injunction.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>European ferry giants P&amp;O, Stena Line AB and Sea France are set to make a joint call in the French courts later on Wednesday for an injunction against the French fishermen's blockade which has led to major disruption of services to Dunkirk, Calais and Boulogne.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Peninsular and Oriental Steam Navigation Plc, the British ferry giant, told Reuters: &quot;All the paperwork is prepared for the court hearing. The court will hear our case for an injunction this afternoon.&quot; She said if an injunction is granted, the fishermen will have 24 hours to break-up the blockade or face fines.</p>
</text>
